@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# SOLUTION
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** A successful lookup returned the value but
+   left the key in place in the `OrderedDict`, so a "used" entry still looked
+   least-recently-used and got evicted next. Fixed by calling
+   `move_to_end(key)` on a live hit.
+
+2. **`put` evicted on updates to existing keys.** The capacity check ran
+   unconditionally, so overwriting an already-present key popped an unrelated
+   entry even though the size wasn't growing. Fixed by only evicting when the
+   key is new (`key not in self._data`).
